# Model behavior

**CONSTRAINT:** These rules are universal. MUST apply on every turn that produces written output or uses the filesystem. MUST NOT skip chat replies or file edits.

Human interaction: `.cursor/rules/always-rules-01-human-interaction.mdc`.

## Language (code and docs)

- MUST use English only for code, identifiers, comments, strings, paths, and documentation.
- MUST use **US English** spelling in generated prose and in chat when not quoting the author.
- MUST use one consistent English term per concept in code and docs.
- MUST NOT use non-English text in the codebase.
- Example: use `userName` and `getData()`; do not use mixed-language identifiers or comments.

Chat replies are owned by `always-rules-01-human-interaction.mdc` (fluent consultant, light tutor). MUST NOT apply a telegraph quota (first-8-words, one idea, at most 3 sentences) to chat.

## Punctuation (all written output)

- MUST NOT use the em dash character (U+2014) in any written output: chat responses, generated files, `tmp/`, social posts, or docs. Use comma, semicolon, colon, or parentheses instead.

## Library source for debugging

- MAY clone upstream into `tmp/<library-name>` to read or debug. MUST NOT modify or commit to upstream repos. MUST keep clones out of unrelated paths.

## Git branch before file changes

**CONSTRAINT:** Before creating work that changes files in a git repository, MUST check the current branch. If HEAD is a default branch, MUST create and switch to a short descriptive feature branch first. MUST NOT edit project files while on a default branch.

- Default branch names: `main`, `master`, `develop`, `trunk`
- If detached HEAD: leave as-is; create a feature branch only when HEAD names a default branch
- New branch names (when creating from a default branch): short descriptive kebab-case with a `feat/` or `fix/` prefix (example: `feat/timeout-guard`)
- Branch rename is optional; the open PR tip matters more than the branch label

Enforcement: run `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` (or equivalent) before the first file edit in a turn that will change files
Violation: STOP, create/switch to a feature branch, then continue

CORRECT:
```text
HEAD is main; task will edit files
→ git checkout -b feat/add-branch-guard
→ then edit files
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
HEAD is main, master, develop, or trunk
→ edit files on that branch
```

**CONSTRAINT:** When HEAD is already a non-default branch, MUST stay on that branch for continuing related work. MUST NOT create a sibling `feat/`/`fix/` branch only because the task title changed.

Enforcement: before `git checkout -b` / `git switch -c` on a non-default HEAD, confirm the user asked to split or start after merge
Violation: STOP, stay on the current branch (or run the open-PR gate below)

CORRECT:
```text
HEAD is feat/context-reading-path; next slice continues the same capability
→ stay on feat/context-reading-path; commit there
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
HEAD is feat/context-reading-path; next slice continues the same capability
→ git checkout -b feat/door-walk-cluster-seed
→ open a second PR
```

**CONSTRAINT:** Before the first file edit on a non-default branch, MUST check for an open pull request for that branch (`gh pr list --head <branch> --state open`, or equivalent). If an open PR exists and the user has not already chosen in this conversation, MUST ask one real fork and wait:

1. Continue on the current open PR (keep committing there; after meaningful pushes, update the PR summary to match the full capability)
2. Finish the merge first, then start a new branch from the default branch

MUST NOT open a sibling PR for a capability build-up without that choice. MUST NOT invent a stacked PR trail (`#25`, `#26`, `#27`) for one unfinished capability.

Enforcement: `gh pr list --head "$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD)" --state open` (or equivalent) before edits when HEAD is non-default; if open and no prior choice, ask and wait
Violation: STOP, ask the fork, do not `checkout -b` and do not `gh pr create`

CORRECT:
```text
HEAD is feat/context-reading-path; open PR #25; next work continues the capability
→ Ask: continue on PR #25 (then update summary) or merge first and start fresh?
→ User picks continue
→ stay on the branch; push; update PR #25 summary
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
HEAD is feat/context-reading-path; open PR #25
→ git checkout -b feat/findings-pr-comment-threads
→ gh pr create
→ leave #25 unmerged
```
